{"id": "q0010", "pool": "frozen", "arm": "local", "tier": "never", "lang": "en", "run_id": "ttfa1", "attempt": 1, "seed": 2992997385, "protocol": "ttfa-v3", "config_sha256": "923cbbdfe3213927dfa36b1f8e0eb48a30d641d9b9bf7cf25d16765340d88836", "gate_art_sha256": "0e6494c2eeac9bcd86c10b5def3cbd32e98bb0765fa2fd8afc8c1b47915ea372", "threshold": null, "gpu": "NVIDIA H100 80GB HBM3", "host": "modal", "shard": 3, "query": "In November, a toy was $40. In December, the price increased by 80%. In January, the price decreased by 50%. What was the price of the toy after it was discounted in January?\n\nShow your work and end with the final numeric answer.", "input_path": "/data/audio_pool/q0010.wav", "input_sha256": "4ae53f05706a64f084a4ee706c6742b88e8096bc8de8cae092ccdd3910366db6", "input_samples": 241600, "input_s": 15.1, "n_real_chunks": 16, "score": 0.3061, "act": 0.9974, "is_info": true, "fired": false, "mode": "local", "answer": "Let's break this down step by step. In November, the toy cost $40. Then, in December, it increased by 80%. An 80% increase means we add 80% of $40 to the original price. So, that is 0.8 times 4 0, which equal s $32 added on. That makes the new price $ 4 0 plus $3 2, so $7 2 in December. Now, in January, the price decreased by 50%. A 5 0% decrease from $ 72 means we take half of that amount off. Half of 72 is 3 6. So, subtracting 36 from 7 2 gives us $36. Therefore, after the discount in January, the price of the toy was $36.", "relay_text": "", "expert_answer": "", "transcript": "", "asr_s": null, "expert_s": null, "expert_input_samples": null, "expert_input_s": null, "expert_input_sha256": null, "expert_timed_out": false, "wait_s": null, "relay_synth_ms": null, "onset_chunk": 15, "eot_seen": true, "n_speak_chunks": 51, "feed_lag_max_ms": 47, "feed_lag_sum_ms": 67, "audio_files": {"local": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/frozen/audio/q0010_local_local.wav", "sha256": "f44770292ae6bbecc7b17f3502ae4d5524a4d2b4f09482709839f9ee2314050b", "sr": 24000, 