{"id": "q0080", "pool": "frozen", "arm": "local", "tier": "never", "lang": "en", "run_id": "ttfa1", "attempt": 1, "seed": 1671905088, "protocol": "ttfa-v3", "config_sha256": "923cbbdfe3213927dfa36b1f8e0eb48a30d641d9b9bf7cf25d16765340d88836", "gate_art_sha256": "0e6494c2eeac9bcd86c10b5def3cbd32e98bb0765fa2fd8afc8c1b47915ea372", "threshold": null, "gpu": "NVIDIA H100 80GB HBM3", "host": "modal", "shard": 3, "query": "Janet goes to the mall and spends $3.50 on ice cream, $7.50 each for movie tickets for herself and her younger sister, and $8.50 on a bracelet. If her parents gave her $40, how many dollars does she have left?\n\nShow your work and end with the final numeric answer.", "input_path": "/data/audio_pool/q0080.wav", "input_sha256": "2bcd82a1296ff86c08971d2469733596596a17403b72985b882c9a2546c326a9", "input_samples": 294400, "input_s": 18.4, "n_real_chunks": 19, "score": 0.2067, "act": 0.9989, "is_info": true, "fired": false, "mode": "local", "answer": "So she spends 3 dollars and 50 cents on ice cream, plus 7 dollars and 5 0 cents each for two movie tickets, which is 15 dollars total, plus 8 dollars and 5 0 cents on a bracelet. That adds up to 27 dollars in total spent. If her parents gave her 40 dollars, then subtracting the amount spent from what she was given gives us 40 minus 2 7, which equal s 13 dollars left. So, Janet has 13 dollars left.", "relay_text": "", "expert_answer": "", "transcript": "", "asr_s": null, "expert_s": null, "expert_input_samples": null, "expert_input_s": null, "expert_input_sha256": null, "expert_timed_out": false, "wait_s": null, "relay_synth_ms": null, "onset_chunk": 18, "eot_seen": true, "n_speak_chunks": 28, "feed_lag_max_ms": 0, "feed_lag_sum_ms": 0, "audio_files": {"local": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/frozen/audio/q0080_local_local.wav", "sha256": "ff1e55ca091084b4fb370e341e44602be3cbc21810b0b5ca1f5e2599510ba691", "sr": 24000, "seconds": 28.28}}, "chunks": [[0, 1, 1.0, 1.055, 1.099, 1, 0, 0], [1, 1, 2.0, 2.057, 2.103, 1, 0