{"id": "q0217", "pool": "frozen", "arm": "local", "tier": "never", "lang": "en", "run_id": "ttfa1", "attempt": 1, "seed": 797296068, "protocol": "ttfa-v3", "config_sha256": "923cbbdfe3213927dfa36b1f8e0eb48a30d641d9b9bf7cf25d16765340d88836", "gate_art_sha256": "0e6494c2eeac9bcd86c10b5def3cbd32e98bb0765fa2fd8afc8c1b47915ea372", "threshold": null, "gpu": "NVIDIA H100 80GB HBM3", "host": "modal", "shard": 3, "query": "An engine running at 1100 rpm drives a line shaft by means of a belt. The engine pulley has a 9 in. diameter and 25 hp has to be transmitted. The coefficient of friction y between the belt and pulley material is 0.25. Determine, whether the belt slip is possible for the following angles of contact: (a) 150° (b) 100°\n\nA. The belt will slip at both 150° and 100°.\nB. The belt slip is independent of the angle of contact.\nC. The belt will not slip at 150° but tends to slip at 100°.\nD. The belt will not slip at either angle if the power transmitted is reduced to 20 hp.\nE. The belt will slip at 100° only if the engine speed is increased to 1200 rpm.\nF. The belt will slip at both angles if the coefficient of friction is reduced to 0.20.\nG. The belt will not slip at both 150° and 100°.\nH. The belt will not slip at 100° but tends to slip at 150°.\nI. The belt will slip at 150° if the power transmitted exceeds 30 hp.\nJ. The belt will slip at 150° but not at 100°.\n\nAnswer with the correct option letter and its content.", "input_path": "/data/audio_pool/q0217.wav", "input_sha256": "90d4a531ac6844ab8458f7039ff4264edb3f35a9a4c88c479a12a7e07dc40d88", "input_samples": 1200800, "input_s": 75.05, "n_real_chunks": 76, "score": 0.9207, "act": 0.9987, "is_info": true, "fired": false, "mode": "local", "answer": "Let's see. We have an engine running at 1,100 RP M driving a line shaft via belt. The engine pul ley has a 9-inch diameter and we need to transmit 2 5 hp. The coefficient of friction is 0.2 5. So the question is whether slip is possible for different contact angles. I think this one depends on the power transmitted versus what the belt can handle without slipping. If the power is too high relative to the friction and angle, it will slip. Looking at the options, option A says slip at both angles, B says independent of angle, C says no slip at 1 50 but tends to slip at 100, D says no slip if power is reduced to 20 h p, E says slip only at 100 if speed increases, F says slip at both if friction drops to 0. 2, G says no slip at both angles, H says no slip at 100 but tends to slip at 15 0, I says slip at 15 0 if power exceeds 30 hp, J says slip at 150 but not at 100. Given that 2 5 hp is being transmitted, and assuming the belt grip is sufficient for those angles with the given friction, typically larger contact angles allow", "relay_text": "", "expert_answer": "", "transcript": "", "asr_s": null, "expert_s": null, "expert_input_samples": null, "expert_input_s": null, "expert_input_sha256": null, "expert_timed_out": false, "wait_s": null, "relay_synth_ms": null, "onset_chunk": 75, "eot_seen": false, "n_speak_chunks": 60, "feed_lag_max_ms": 65, "feed_lag_sum_ms": 65, "audio_files": {"local": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/frozen/audio/q0217_local_local.wav", "sha256": "16353873acc660c1a88c6a534e3d68e272bbcd36858214b6feb76d9345ce8d1a", "sr": 24000, "seconds": 60.0}}, "chunks": [[0, 1, 1.0, 1.055, 1.102, 1, 0, 0], [1, 1, 2.0, 2.06, 2.108, 1, 0, 0], [2, 1, 3.0, 3.058, 3.106, 1, 0, 0], [3, 1, 4.0, 4.06, 4.109, 1, 0, 0], [4, 1, 5.0, 5.06, 5.109, 1, 0, 0], [5, 1, 6.0, 6.058, 6.106, 1, 0, 0], [6, 1, 7.0, 7.056, 7.104, 1, 0, 0], [7, 1, 8.0, 8.057, 8.105, 1, 0, 0], [8, 1, 9.0, 9.059, 9.108, 1, 0, 0], [9, 1, 10.0, 10.058, 10.105, 1, 0, 0], [10, 1, 11.0, 11.056, 11.105, 1, 0, 0], [11, 1, 12.0, 12.059, 12.108, 1, 0, 0], [12, 1, 13.0, 13.059, 13.107, 1, 0, 0], [13, 1, 14.0, 14.059, 14.107, 1, 0, 0], [14, 1, 15.0, 15.059, 15.112, 1, 0, 0], [15, 1, 16.0, 16.06, 16.108, 1, 0, 0], [16, 1, 17.0, 17.056, 17.105, 1, 0, 0], [17, 1, 18.0, 18.06, 