{"id": "q0287", "pool": "frozen", "arm": "local", "tier": "never", "lang": "en", "run_id": "ttfa1", "attempt": 1, "seed": 4266098317, "protocol": "ttfa-v3", "config_sha256": "923cbbdfe3213927dfa36b1f8e0eb48a30d641d9b9bf7cf25d16765340d88836", "gate_art_sha256": "0e6494c2eeac9bcd86c10b5def3cbd32e98bb0765fa2fd8afc8c1b47915ea372", "threshold": null, "gpu": "NVIDIA H100 80GB HBM3", "host": "modal", "shard": 3, "query": "A sofa has a markup of 20% based on its selling price. Find the percent markup based on the cost.\n\nA. 28%\nB. 15%\nC. 22%\nD. 10%\nE. 30%\nF. 20%\nG. 40%\nH. 18%\nI. 25%\nJ. 35%\n\nAnswer with the correct option letter and its content.", "input_path": "/data/audio_pool/q0287.wav", "input_sha256": "7a3d3df789a585608e37c59fddf786d50fae79a2d747736b54bb1b0162dd4c11", "input_samples": 276600, "input_s": 17.288, "n_real_chunks": 18, "score": 0.558, "act": 0.9986, "is_info": true, "fired": false, "mode": "local", "answer": "So if the mark up is 20 percent based on selling price, then that means that the cost plus 2 0% of the cost equal s the selling price. Let' s say C is the cost and S is the selling price. So we have C plus 0. 2C equal s S. That gives us 1.2 C equals S. We want to find the percent mark up based on cost, so let's solve for it. If I divide both sides by C, I get 1.2 equals S over C. Then I can subtract 1 from both sides to get 0.2 equals S over C minus 1, which is just S over C minus 1. That means the mark up as a fraction of cost is 0.2, or 20%. But wait, that's not right because 0.2 times 10 0 is actually 20%, but that' s the same as the given mark up. No, no, no, hold on. Actually, let me think again. If 1. 2C equals S, then S is 1.2 times C. That means the selling price is 120% of the cost. So the mark up is 2 0% of the cost. Oh! Wait, that's exactly what they said? No, no, no, hang on. The question says the mark up is 2 0% based", "relay_text": "", "expert_answer": "", "transcript": "", "asr_s": null, "expert_s": null, "expert_input_sampl